---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Flynn Lin',
  url: 'https://ufo-declassified.com/about/flynn-lin',
  jobTitle: 'Founder & Editor',
  worksFor: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'UFO Declassified',
    url: 'https://ufo-declassified.com',
  },
  knowsAbout: [
    'Declassified U.S. government documents',
    'UAP / UFO history',
    'PURSUE initiative',
    'Science fiction film and television',
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Flynn Lin"
  description="About Flynn Lin — founder and editor of UFO Declassified. Independent developer, lifelong science fiction reader, and UAP document archivist."
  ogType="article"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} slot="head" />

  <section class="container-narrow py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[10px] text-space-300 mb-6 font-mono tracking-wider uppercase">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-cyan-bright transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/about" class="hover:text-cyan-bright transition-colors">About</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-space-100">Flynn Lin</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="section-header">
      <h1 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Flynn Lin</h1>
      <p class="text-cyan-bright text-xs font-mono tracking-widest uppercase mt-2">Founder & Editor</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 text-space-200 text-sm mt-8">

      <p>
        <strong class="text-white">Flynn Lin</strong> is the founder, editor, and sole operator of
        UFO Declassified. He built and maintains the archive, writes the analysis articles, and curates
        every record page on the site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Background</h2>
      <p>
        Flynn has been fascinated with the unknown since childhood. Growing up in China, he read every
        issue of <em class="text-white">Feidie Tansuo</em> (飞碟探索, "UFO Exploration") — a monthly
        magazine that was, for years, the country's only mainstream publication dedicated to UFO
        reporting and investigation. That magazine taught him to treat sightings as data to be
        organized rather than mysteries to be sensationalized — an approach that directly shapes how
        UFO Declassified is structured today.
      </p>
      <p>
        His favorite filmmaker is <strong class="text-white">Steven Spielberg</strong>, and
        <em class="text-white">Close Encounters of the Third Kind</em> (1977) remains the single most
        formative film of his life — not for its aliens, but for its patient, ordinary protagonist who
        simply refuses to look away from something he cannot explain. He is also a longtime fan of the
        American miniseries <em class="text-white">Taken</em> (2002), which traced a single family's
        encounter across generations and reinforced his belief that the human story around UAP matters
        as much as the technical record.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Why This Site Exists</h2>
      <p>
        By day, Flynn is an independent developer and website operator. When the U.S. government
        launched the PURSUE initiative in May 2026 and began releasing declassified UAP records through
        war.gov/UFO, he found the official portal powerful but hard to navigate — large file sizes,
        inconsistent naming, and no contextual analysis. UFO Declassified is his attempt to fix that:
        a searchable, citable, human-readable archive built by one person who cares about getting the
        source material right.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Editorial Approach</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2">
        <li><strong class="text-white">Primary sources first.</strong> Every record page links back to the original government file.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">No sensationalism.</strong> Analysis is clearly separated from fact; interpretation is labeled as such.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">Citation-ready.</strong> Each page is structured so researchers and journalists can cite it directly.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">Corrections welcome.</strong> Errors are fixed promptly — see the <a href="/contact" class="text-cyan-bright hover:underline">contact page</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Connect</h2>
      <p>
        Reach Flynn directly at <a href="mailto:contact@ufo-declassified.com" class="text-cyan-bright hover:underline">contact@ufo-declassified.com</a>
        for corrections, tips, media inquiries, or questions about any record on this site.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
